## PREFACE AND SCOPE NOTICE

This document specifies the RTL Standardization & Normalization subsystem of the dataset engineering pipeline described across Phase 14.1 through the present phase. It defines the architecture, policies, transformation rules, metadata contracts, and validation strategy required to convert heterogeneous benchmark RTL — acquired and license-cleared under Phase 14.2 — into a reproducible, synthesis-ready RTL representation suitable for consumption by Phase 14.5 (Logic Synthesis).

This document does **not** redefine, restate, or modify any policy established in Phases 14.1–14.3. Where this specification depends on artifacts, identifiers, or conventions introduced in earlier phases (`benchmark_id`, `version_tag`, dataset manifest schema, checksum philosophy, four-axis versioning), those definitions are treated as fixed inputs and are referenced, not reproduced.

This document explicitly excludes the following, each of which is reserved for its own phase:

- Logic synthesis, technology mapping, or gate-level netlist generation (Phase 14.5)
- Feature extraction of any kind, node/edge/spatial/global (a later phase)
- Ground-truth label generation (covered exclusively in Phase 14.3)
- Placement, routing, or any physical design step
- Any ML model architecture, training procedure, or inference pipeline

The RTL Standardization & Normalization subsystem occupies a narrow, precisely bounded position in the pipeline: it accepts acquired RTL as an immutable input and produces a normalized, synthesis-ready RTL derivative as its sole output, together with the metadata, logs, and validation artifacts required to make that transformation auditable and reproducible at the scale required for large benchmark corpora and multi-PDK dataset generation campaigns.

