## CHAPTER 6 — INPUTS

### 6.1 Purpose

This chapter fixes the exact input contract consumed by the RTL Standardization & Normalization subsystem.

### 6.2 Inputs

- The acquired RTL source tree for a given `benchmark_id`/`version_tag`, as delivered unmodified by Phase 14.2.
- The Phase 14.2 acquisition manifest entry corresponding to that benchmark, including license classification, checksum record, and RTL-language declaration.
- The Phase 14.4 Standardization Configuration, a versioned, benchmark-agnostic policy document specifying active transformation rules, naming conventions, and eligibility thresholds (this configuration is itself a versioned artifact under the four-axis versioning pattern established in Phase 14.3).

### 6.3 Dependencies

This stage has a hard dependency on the completion and validation of the corresponding Phase 14.2 acquisition record; no benchmark may enter standardization prior to acquisition sign-off, preserving pipeline stage ordering established in Phase 14.1.

### 6.4 Failure Conditions

Absence of a valid acquisition manifest entry, checksum mismatch against the Phase 14.2 record, or an undeclared/unsupported RTL language (Chapter 9) each constitute an ingestion failure, causing the benchmark to be logged as rejected-at-ingestion rather than silently skipped.

### 6.5 Reviewer Expectations

Reviewers will expect explicit confirmation that this stage performs a checksum re-verification against Phase 14.2 records prior to any processing, closing the audit loop between phases.

